WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:01.440
In this video series,

00:00:01.440 --> 00:00:07.040
we take a deep dive into maximally
lowering LDL cholesterol through diet,

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:10.080
as LDL is the primary driver
of our primary killer

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:12.640
and the lower, the better.

00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:16.880
We'll talk about expanding
the portfolio diet,

00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:19.520
talk about plant sterols,
cholesterol-lowering supplements,

00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:21.680
foods, herbs, spices—
you name it—

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:25.520
ending up with a Dr. Greger
in-the-kitchen type video

00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:29.120
where I share how to make this
cholesterol-lowering powder

00:00:29.120 --> 00:00:30.720
you can sprinkle on foods.

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:33.840
Anyway, if you don't want to wait
for each video to be released,

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:36.880
I've compiled all the information
into a brand new book

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:41.218
available at nutritionfacts.org/books.

00:00:41.572 --> 00:00:48.000
"How to Lower Cholesterol with the Portfolio Diet"

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:50.480
Of the top ten
take-home messages

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:53.440
for the primary prevention
of cardiovascular disease,

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:54.400
take-home number nine

00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:56.480
is that cholesterol-lowering
statin drugs

00:00:56.480 --> 00:00:58.480
are considered
the first-choice drug treatment

00:00:58.480 --> 00:01:00.160
for preventing heart disease
in those

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:03.600
with sufficiently elevated
LDL cholesterol,

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:06.080
though side effects,
like muscle pain or weakness,

00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:09.520
may impact up to a quarter
of users.

00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:11.840
Regardless, whether you
and your doctor decide

00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:14.720
to start drugs,
the number one take-home message

00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:17.600
is that the most important way
to prevent heart disease—

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:19.600
the number one killer
of men and women—

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:22.480
is to promote a healthy
lifestyle throughout life.

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:24.720
Enter the Portfolio Diet

00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:28.240
for the maximal reduction
of LDL cholesterol.

00:01:28.240 --> 00:01:30.400
There are three main
added factors in our diet

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:32.320
that raise LDL cholesterol:

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:36.560
trans fat, saturated fat,
and dietary cholesterol.

00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:38.480
Therefore, the tolerable
upper intake levels

00:01:38.480 --> 00:01:40.800
of these three factors
are essentially zero,

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:42.480
since any intake above zero

00:01:42.480 --> 00:01:44.800
increases LDL
cholesterol concentration

00:01:44.800 --> 00:01:48.640
and therefore increases risk
of coronary heart disease.

00:01:48.640 --> 00:01:51.520
So, trans fat, saturated fat,
and cholesterol intake

00:01:51.520 --> 00:01:53.840
should be as low as possible.

00:01:53.840 --> 00:01:56.240
That means cutting back
as much as possible

00:01:56.240 --> 00:02:01.360
on meat, dairy, eggs, and junk.

00:02:01.360 --> 00:02:03.280
And since
partially hydrogenated oils

00:02:03.280 --> 00:02:06.000
must be removed from
the U.S. food supply by law,

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:08.480
all these other uses
have been banned;

00:02:08.480 --> 00:02:10.560
so, animal products
are now the leading source

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:13.680
of trans fat
in the U.S. diet as well.

00:02:13.680 --> 00:02:16.480
Those eating a Western diet
have circulating LDL levels

00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:19.440
around 120 milligrams
per deciliter.

00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:22.000
No surprise, then,
that those eating plant-based

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:23.760
tend to have lower LDL,

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:25.680
with lower levels the longer
they have been eating

00:02:25.680 --> 00:02:27.600
a whole food,
plant-based diet;

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:29.600
as low as 70,

00:02:29.600 --> 00:02:31.360
but even though
that's an excellent number

00:02:31.360 --> 00:02:33.200
compared to most people,

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:35.440
if you remember
from a previous video,

00:02:35.440 --> 00:02:37.840
there really isn't
a safe cutoff.

00:02:37.840 --> 00:02:39.360
When it comes to LDL,

00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:41.440
the lower the longer,
the better,

00:02:41.440 --> 00:02:43.520
even if you're at low risk.

00:02:43.520 --> 00:02:45.600
That's where the Portfolio Diet
can come in.

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:47.760
By eating
a healthy plant-based diet,

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:50.080
you've already subtracted
all the major foods

00:02:50.080 --> 00:02:52.160
that increase your cholesterol.

00:02:52.160 --> 00:02:55.840
The Portfolio Diet is
a plant-based diet with a bonus,

00:02:55.840 --> 00:02:57.920
a "portfolio" of foods—

00:02:57.920 --> 00:03:00.080
four food types you can add
to your diet

00:03:00.080 --> 00:03:03.200
to pull cholesterol
out of your system.

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:04.480
The food components include

00:03:04.480 --> 00:03:06.480
one and a half ounces of nuts
(42 g) a day,

00:03:06.480 --> 00:03:07.840
good sources of plant protein,

00:03:07.840 --> 00:03:10.720
in other words, legumes,
like soy, other beans,

00:03:10.720 --> 00:03:13.280
split-peas, chickpeas,
or lentils,

00:03:13.280 --> 00:03:14.880
lots of food
with viscous fiber,

00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:17.280
that's the kind of slimy fiber
found in oats, okra,

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:19.600
eggplant, barley,
and ground flax seeds,

00:03:19.600 --> 00:03:21.840
and finally two grams a day
of plant sterols

00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:23.920
from fortified foods
or supplements.

00:03:23.920 --> 00:03:26.640
Dr. Greger is going to take
a deep dive into phytosterols;

00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:29.200
but first, let's just see
what this diet can do.

00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:31.680
The Portfolio Diet
was tested head-to-head

00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:32.800
against statin treatment

00:03:32.800 --> 00:03:34.560
plus a very low
saturated fat diet,

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:36.480
in a four-week randomized
controlled trial

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:38.720
among people
with high cholesterol.

00:03:38.720 --> 00:03:41.360
And incredibly, those
in the Portfolio Diet group

00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:44.720
had nearly a 30% drop
in LDL cholesterol–

00:03:44.720 --> 00:03:48.320
similar to the 33% drop
observed in the statins

00:03:48.320 --> 00:03:50.960
plus low saturated fat group.

00:03:50.960 --> 00:03:52.720
Simply by emphasizing
the addition

00:03:52.720 --> 00:03:54.400
of four dietary components

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:57.520
that are each likely
to contribute 4% to 7%

00:03:57.520 --> 00:03:59.760
to overall
cholesterol reduction,

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:02.320
you have a diet
that reduces LDL cholesterol

00:04:02.320 --> 00:04:05.440
with drug-like potency.

00:04:05.440 --> 00:04:07.280
In a systematic review
and meta-analysis

00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:09.520
of controlled trials
of the Portfolio Diet,

00:04:09.520 --> 00:04:12.400
we still see consistent
LDL-lowering benefits,

00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:14.960
about a 17% drop
above and beyond

00:04:14.960 --> 00:04:17.360
the currently recommended
relatively strict

00:04:17.360 --> 00:04:20.400
National Cholesterol
Education Program Step 2 diet,

00:04:21.120 --> 00:04:23.360
along with lowering
of systemic inflammation

00:04:23.360 --> 00:04:28.080
and an estimated 13% decrease
in ten-year heart disease risk.

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:30.000
And these results
weren't even in individuals

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:32.560
who all actually went
on a Portfolio Diet;

00:04:32.560 --> 00:04:35.200
they were merely told
to eat that way.

00:04:35.200 --> 00:04:37.760
Even just two educational
sessions over six months

00:04:37.760 --> 00:04:41.120
telling people to adopt it
can have a significant effect.

00:04:41.120 --> 00:04:42.720
I mentioned
the four food components,

00:04:42.720 --> 00:04:44.880
but what does a sample menu
look like?

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:46.240
Nuts for snacks;

00:04:46.240 --> 00:04:48.560
soy foods and beans
for plant protein;

00:04:48.560 --> 00:04:51.360
oats, barley, okra, eggplant,
Metamucil, and oranges

00:04:51.360 --> 00:04:53.120
for soluble fiber;

00:04:53.120 --> 00:04:55.200
and what's all
this margarine for?

00:04:55.200 --> 00:04:57.920
They were using plant
sterol-fortified margarine,

00:04:57.920 --> 00:05:00.080
like Benecol
and Promise Activ,

00:05:00.080 --> 00:05:02.640
formerly known as Take Control.

00:05:02.640 --> 00:05:05.120
Yes, they have added
plant sterols,

00:05:05.120 --> 00:05:08.000
but they're also chock-full
of salt, saturated fat,

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:09.600
and artificial flavors.

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:12.320
I mean, if you're going to use
some sort of spread,

00:05:12.320 --> 00:05:14.640
this would be better than
non-sterol fortified margarine

00:05:14.640 --> 00:05:15.600
or butter,

00:05:15.600 --> 00:05:18.960
but seems like a strange way
to prevent heart disease.

00:05:18.960 --> 00:05:20.720
Plant sterols are
naturally concentrated

00:05:20.720 --> 00:05:22.480
in sesame seeds and wheat germ

00:05:22.480 --> 00:05:25.840
and also found in a variety
of grains and legumes.

00:05:25.840 --> 00:05:28.800
To get that recommended two
or three grams a day, though,

00:05:28.800 --> 00:05:32.000
you may have to take
plant sterol supplements.

00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:34.800
In fact, should we all
be doing that?

00:05:34.800 --> 00:05:36.800
That's what Dr. Greger
will tackle next,

00:05:36.800 --> 00:05:38.160
and then see
if there's any other

00:05:38.160 --> 00:05:41.360
cholesterol-lowering supplements
that might be worth taking.

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:43.200
Finally,
what about all the other foods

00:05:43.200 --> 00:05:45.280
that lower cholesterol?

00:05:45.280 --> 00:05:47.120
What about expanding
our portfolio

00:05:47.120 --> 00:05:49.600
to make some kind
of Portfolio Plus Diet

00:05:49.600 --> 00:05:51.600
with as many different
cholesterol-lowering foods

00:05:51.600 --> 00:05:54.560
and herbs and spices as we can?

00:05:54.560 --> 00:05:57.360
Again, not as a replacement
for drugs,

00:05:57.360 --> 00:06:00.640
but as a way to drive our LDL
as low as possible

00:06:00.640 --> 00:06:02.640
with our fridge and pantry

00:06:02.640 --> 00:06:04.640
in addition to anything
we might have

00:06:04.640 --> 00:06:07.293
in our medicine cabinet.

